  "2026-10-21T18:09:55.584Z",codex-agent,"The full benchmark and revert workflow passed at 124975a. Verified all 81 rows, 1620 measured samples and successful exits for all 27 oracle cases; the exact before/after tables are persisted on this item (apart from the CLI standard trailing-whitespace trim) and in docs. At 50k, native comment p50/p95 is 62.9/63.8 ms versus before 762.4/766.0; update is 62.8/64.0 versus 760.5/770.1. Claim peak RSS is 25080 KiB versus 508528, with p50 2585.6 ms versus 3836.3. Oracle claim/search/list remain faster at this scale; current-oracle byte comparisons are reported rather than assumed. Linux aggregate passed 524 ordinary plus 524 instrumented tests and 100 percent lines/functions/regions, then correctly refused its sole missed branch (3159/3160). The passing new fallback unit case exercises exactly that filename-boundary false arm. No production Rust, threshold or exclusion changed after the measured source. Next step is committing this test-only repair with the receipts and verifying the final full matrix."
  "2026-10-21T18:45:34.986Z",codex-agent,"All exact-head CI gates passed at fd836ba: Linux 525 ordinary + 525 instrumented tests, macOS 521 + 521, Windows 516 + 516, each aggregate across 42 suite executions with zero failed or ignored tests. Every platform measures 100 percent lines/functions/regions/branches; Linux totals are 13218 lines, 1370 functions, 22077 regions and 3160 branches, all covered. Formatting, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, audit under the existing allowed advisory policy, changelog and documented fresh-clone tracker preflight passed. All nine unchanged latency bounds passed. The full benchmark and both revert controls also passed again at fd836ba, with 1620 measured samples; the before/native executables are byte-identical to the committed measurement run. Receipts: docs/benchmarks/native-hot-path-gates-2026-10-21.json and native-hot-path-reproduction-2026-10-21.json. The optional local environment health preflight remains separate and reports shared clone-configuration drift; that configuration is untouched under the no-merge-work boundary. No universal native speed or current-oracle parity claim is made: claim/search/list still trail the oracle at 50k, next/list-open are absent, and context refuses 10k+. Release ownership for orchestrator review; keep every item open and PR 102 unmerged. The final documentary commit will receive an exact-head CI check, recorded in PR 102."
  "2026-10-21T18:58:43.699Z",codex-agent,"PR #101 merged during validation. Integrating the merged 2026.10.21 parity baseline before fresh measurements and unchanged release gates. Earlier benchmark receipts remain scoped to their recorded source. Retaining all durability checks, strict unrelated-item validation and the 50-writer no-git contract."
